String => sequence of characters are called string
          define with double quotes
          String is object(non -primitive data type)
          It immutable can't change -> any modification create new string
          ex:  "hello" => "hello world" => old string still exists in memory

Memory for storing:

        String constant Pool(SCP)

        ex: String a = "abc";
            String b = "abc";
            Only one object is created a,b both are denoting the same;


StringBuffer:

  its mutable
  that means you can modify the same object
  no new object creation for change.

  ex:

  StringBuffer str = new StringBuffer("Hello");
  str.append("world)";

  "Hello world" => same object

when to use?

string => when string is constant no frequent changes are needed.
StringBuffer => when loop-based changes

why?
string => immutable
  security => file paths , urls
  Thread safety

 String builder => mutable , it's not thread safed , but faster performance


